 "notes": "GT also defines an S3 read document that is not part of the effective policy, so it is not checked. 'Only' that secret is checked via scope ref, not a no-other-action check. Policy text is unknown at plan, hence declared branches. Read grant must be secretsmanager:GetSecretValue bound to the named inline policy (its own text, or the policy document it references); a bare secretsmanager:* is not 'reading only'. Role name accepts name or name_prefix (candidate review: Gemini38F uses name_prefix). Residual gap: an inline JSON policy that grants the secret plus Resource \"*\" still passes the scope check (no negation over policy strings)."
